            <ArticleTitle>A clinical overview of removable prostheses: 5. Diagnosis and treatment of RPD problems.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-94, 96-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This, the fifth and final article in the series, addresses the diagnoses and treatment of problems which may arise following provision of removable partial dentures (RPDs). These include difficulties seating the denture, pain and discomfort, looseness and functional problems.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
